cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this verification, please cite it as below."
title: "Pilus: independent kernel-level verification of a claimed negative resolution of Erdős Problem 486"
abstract: >-
  Artifacts of a third-party replay of the Lean 4 formalization
  accompanying a claimed negative resolution of Erdős Problem 486: a
  mechanical axiom sweep over every theorem in the development, an
  external lean4checker replay of the compiled environment, an
  exact-arithmetic corroboration of the construction's constants, and a
  from-source bootstrap script. Includes machine-checked findings that
  the formal-conjectures statement of Problem 486 is degenerate for two
  independent reasons and that the obvious repair does not fix it. The
  mathematics is due to the claimant; the contribution here is the
  independent verification.
authors:
